        "original_id": "80fb60fb-d506-5b14-a507-5ae10a2b009e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Now Show\n- People: Sue Perkins, Jon Holmes, Laura Shavin, Emma Kennedy, Marcus Brigstocke, Mitch Benn, Pippa Evans, Adam Kay\n- Organizations: BBC Radio 4\n- Places: East Dulwich, south London\n- Roles: comedian, broadcaster, actress, writer\n- Topics: British radio comedy, news satire\n\nFacts:\n- The Now Show is a British radio comedy program broadcast on BBC Radio 4 that satirises the week's news.\n- The Now Show features skits by Jon Holmes and Laura Shavin, while earlier series featured Emma Kennedy or occasionally Sue Perkins for female voices.\n- The Now Show includes a monologue by Marcus Brigstocke and music by Mitch Benn, Pippa Evans, or Adam Kay.\n- Sue Perkins, whose full name is Susan Elizabeth Perkins, was born on 22 September 1969 in East Dulwich, south London.\n- Sue Perkins is an English comedian, broadcaster, actress, and writer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
